# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""Design §21.5 + §14 amendment marker, the charter's third amendments section, ODQ §934.47 addenda 15-16."""
import sys

d, c, f, stamp = sys.argv[1:5]

DESIGN = """

### 21.5 What the execution showed — the recon's report, and the rulings it forces (the chair, __STAMP__; ODQ §934.47 addendum 15; vetoable)

An Opus recon lane EXECUTED the census over the full 525-row golden corpus with two instruments that never disagreed across 525 rows x 22 steps (a recursive counting fork proxy; an in-memory `createPRNG` mint census installed by a loader hook, the tree untouched), and passed its control first: `generatePopulation` draws 315 unpinned and exactly 0 under full pins, and the loader changes no generated byte (the committed golden's own hash). The report, the paste-ready Tier-1 literal and the prototype scripts are in the chair kit (`findings/RECON-EM-P2-CENSUS.report.md`, `findings/RECON-EM-P2-TIER1-LITERAL.md`, `tools/census-prototype/`). **What §21 got right:** execution sees what no spelling can (the alias, every fork receiver, the ambient channel); `(step, key)` dissolves the fork-key arity problem; the row set is total against `getStepMeta()`. **Where §21 was wrong or incomplete — each ruled:**

1. **Tier 1 is 75 rows, not 57** (57 provides entries over 51 distinct keys — five keys have two or three producers: `stress` x3, `stressTypes`, `generationRepairs`, `isolationSupport`, `economicState` — plus 18 `mutates`). 13 of 22 steps draw; 29 rows are drawn, 46 pure. RULED: the row key is `(step, key)` and nothing joins on `key` alone.
2. **`drawn` has a false-positive class: a key that STORES A STREAM LABEL.** `generatePower` draws 0 in 525/525, yet `powerIntent` moves under its perturbation in 525/525 while the settlement stays byte-identical — it carries the seed STRING of a fork. RULED: a row is `drawn` only if the step DRAWS (the counting instrument) AND the key moves; a key that moves under a zero-draw step is classed `label` and named.
3. **THE POWER STRUCTURE CONSUMES NO ENTROPY — so "root means CHOSEN by a draw" (§14) is false of four of EM-A1's ten fields.** `powerStructure` is PURE under every step that touches it; `faction`, `category`, `power`, `governingName`/`isGoverning` move under `resolveStress`, `assembleInstitutions`, `resolveResources`, `cascadePass`, `generateEconomy` — never under `generatePower`. They are COMPUTED from upstream, and the owner's design still, rightly, lets the DM seat a new mayor. RULED — **§14 is amended: an editable root is a fact the record HOLDS, not a fact a draw chose.** The HELD set is the record's first-hand entity facts (the rosters, their identities, attributes, relations and seats); the DERIVED set is the readings over them (scores, states, aggregates, prose). How generation first produced a held fact — `drawn` or `computed` — is RECORDED per row as its `origin`, and is never the test of editability. A pin therefore applies to a computed key exactly as to a drawn one: the record's value is taken and the computation is not run. Tier 2's arm "sits under a drawn key and is entropy-sensitive" is WITHDRAWN; its arms are: the path resolves on a generated record, its holding `(step, key)` is named, its `origin` is measured.
4. **"Reaches the record" has THREE states, and the third is the dangerous one:** absent (5 keys: `generationContentProfile`, `generationContext`, `catalogForTier`, `powerIntent`, `structural`), same, and PRESENT UNDER THE SAME NAME WITH A DIFFERENT VALUE (4 keys: `npcs`, `factions`, `history`, `powerStructure` — `assembleSettlement` enriches them). RULED: the row carries `onRecord: 'absent' | 'same' | 'transformed'`.
5. **⛔ PINNING FROM A RECORD DOES NOT REPRODUCE THE RECORD, and a record-built pin bag is MUTATED IN PLACE.** Pins built from the post-step context reproduce the settlement 9/9; pins built from the RECORD — the only thing the editor ever has — reproduce it 2/9 (the two thorps, where the enrichment is a no-op); and in 3/9 (`corruptionPass`, which draws and writes through the arrays it is handed) the re-derivation WROTE INTO THE CALLER'S OWN RECORD. EM-P0's A2 and A6 cannot see either: they pin from the context, at a config where `corruptionPass` draws 0. RULED: **EM-B2a's premise (`rederive(record, ...)` by pinning from the record through EM-P0's mode) is REFUTED AS DESIGNED and EM-B2a is BLOCKED** pending the re-derivation seam's architecture (ARCH-REDERIVE, below). This is design §14's own provision ("STOPPING with the measured contradiction ... so that a pipeline-seam packet can precede it") firing a train early, which is what the measurement was for.
6. **Drawing into a key a step only MUTATES is the normal mode** (6 of 18 mutates rows, including `corruptionPass` into `npcs`/`factions` in 270/525 — the very keys EM-P0 pins); a drawn key can be OVERWRITTEN before it reaches the record (`generateEconomy`'s `economicState`, drawn 525/525, survives in 332/525); two steps spend entropy that moves nothing declared or undeclared (`isolationPass`, `factionCorrelationPass`). All three are rows' measured facts and ARCH-REDERIVE's inputs.
7. **"Every channel funnels through the stream's `random()`" is FALSE: there is a HASH channel.** `kernel/proseHash.js#pickVariant` makes 96 choices per settlement with zero draws, invisible to counting and to perturbation. RULED: the register declares the hash channel as a second, separately censused channel (the same loader hook over `pickVariant` and the two further `fnv1a32` sites the recon named). ⭐ **It also answers §20.2's owed measurement: YES, a choice is keyed on a DISPLAY NAME** — `assembleInstitutions.js:745` on the seed plus `inst.name` (the institution's description), `npcData.js:1334` on the two NPCs' names (the relationship prose), and `townMap/glyphAssign.js:125` mints `createPRNG('glyph:<name>')`. A rename therefore re-rolls that entity's description, relationship prose and glyph. RULED: those three sites join EM-P1b's class (they key on the stable id once EM-P1 mints it); EM-B1c's rename ops may not be promoted before they do, or the packet names them as its own change; §20.2's immediate rename on canon stands, with this as its named precondition.
8. **A `pure` verdict is only as total as the corpus, and one trial is a one-bit test.** Five `resolveConfig` keys are PURE over all 525 golden rows and DRAWN the moment a config uses the wizard's random modes (`settType:'random'` moves `tier` 19/24 seeds and `townPlus` 11/24; `culture:'random_culture'`; `_randomizePriorities`). RULED: the census corpus is the recon's 63-row sample (every tier x terrain pair once plus all 21 non-grid rows — it reproduces the full classification exactly, 29/29 drawn rows and 13/13 drawing steps, in 23 s against 224 s; every stride sample tested misses `resolveConfig|tradeRoute`) PLUS an off-corpus block built from the wizard's random modes; every `pure` verdict carries the row count behind it; and stream MINTS are censused by execution (35 mints per run against 8 static spellings; one seed minted four times, twice inside other steps), not cited from a static list.

**ARCH-REDERIVE — the open architecture item this creates (the chair's, before EM-B2a can be compiled).** The question is no longer "which steps draw" but "what does it mean to hold a record fixed while the pipeline runs": (a) WHICH VALUE a pin holds for a key the record carries transformed — the step's output (not recoverable from a record) or the record's (then the enrichment must be idempotent, or inverted, or moved behind the pin); (b) PINS ARE FINAL AND ISOLATED — the runner deep-clones pins on entry, no step may write through them, and a pinned key is restored after every step that provides or mutates it; (c) the multi-producer keys (pin the FINAL production) and the mutating drawers (`corruptionPass`: under a pinned roster its pass must not run again); (d) INTRA-STEP dependence among held keys (relationships derive from the NPC roster inside one step, on one stream): what re-derives when ONE held fact changes, without re-rolling its unchanged siblings. A focused Opus recon on `assembleSettlement`'s enrichment and on the held keys' intra-step dependencies precedes the design; EM-P0b is absorbed into it.
"""

CHARTER = """## Amendments of __STAMP__ — the census recon's findings; the pre-proofs' rulings (design §21.5; ODQ §934.47 addenda 15-16)

- **EM-P2 version 3 — the shape is now MEASURED:** Tier 1 = the recon's 75 `(step, key)` rows (the literal is in the chair kit), each with `draws` (the step draws: rows/rows-run), `class: 'drawn' | 'pure' | 'label'` with the row count behind it, `onRecord: 'absent' | 'same' | 'transformed'`, and `via: 'provides' | 'mutates'`; both-directions equal to `getStepMeta()`; the census corpus = the 63-row sample + the off-corpus random-mode block; stream mints and the HASH channel (`pickVariant` + the `fnv1a32` sites) censused by execution through the loader hook. Tier 2 = EM-A1's ten fields re-cut against the live record (the power card is `powerStructure.governingName` + `factions[].isGoverning`, never `seats[].holder`), each row `{ forkId, step, key, module, symbol, outputKey, cardShape, origin: 'drawn' | 'computed' }` — editability is NOT conditioned on entropy (design §14 as amended by §21.5.3).
- **EM-P1b gains three name-keyed choice sites** (design §21.5.7): `assembleInstitutions.js` (`pickVariant` on the seed + `inst.name`), `npcData.js` (on the two NPCs' names), `townMap/glyphAssign.js` (`createPRNG('glyph:<name>')`) — re-keyed on the stable id. **EM-B1c's rename ops are not promoted before it lands** (or the packet names those sites as its own change).
- **EM-B2a is BLOCKED; EM-P0b is ABSORBED into ARCH-REDERIVE** (design §21.5.5 and the item that closes §21.5): pinning from a record reproduces it 2/9 and lets `corruptionPass` write into the caller's record. The chair architects the re-derivation seam (which value a pin holds; pins final and isolated; multi-producer keys; mutating drawers; intra-step dependence) after a focused Opus recon on `assembleSettlement`'s enrichment; the seam's packets precede EM-B2a. EM-D0 and train EM-T7 wait on it with EM-B2a.
- **EM-B3a — THE VEIL PRECEDES THE WRITER:** its `Depends on` is EM-B3b alone; EM-B2a and EM-C1 depend on IT; the two keys' inner shapes are opaque to it. **EM-B3c (NEW, small):** a security walker with a SQL-side subset arm — the net-current gallery scanner must carry every client token's alternative — because a NEW migration re-creating the scanner is invisible to a path-based substrate check.
- **EM-P3 — THE CURE IS THE PLACEMENT:** the citation map leaves `resolveConfig`'s import closure for the domain-reachable leaf (as compiled it put +634 B into the zero-slack worker for bytes the worker never reads); the worker rise that remains rides the standing conditional ruling and is recorded per landing.
- **EM-B1d:** the union-totality walker matches by TOKEN MEMBERSHIP with the foreign unions DECLARED BY NAME, shrink-only, each with its reason and a guard that the exempted file still holds the union it names (`STASIS_REASONS` — captivity is a per-layer fact, design §19 ruling 7; `ENVOY_LOSS_CAUSES`; the verdict union) — a token matcher can only over-report, and a false positive costs a declared row while a miss costs the class; a writer-reach movement is the CHAIR's to bank at the landing (the lane records the walker's verdict and never writes a baseline; growth = STOP); the legacy spellings `'imprisoned'`/`'killed'` becoming AVAILABLE is ratified as inert (no writer ever assigned either to `.status`). At its placement the STALE EM-P2 version 2 is WITHDRAWN to the chair kit (a STALE packet still reserves its change paths; the just-in-time rule).
- **A TENTH REGISTRATION COST, for the whole family (the EM preamble §P2 is amended on the build branch):** a packet that edits any INPUT of an edge-shared bundle closure owes `npm run build:edge-shared` and the regenerated artifacts in its manifest — the test is INPUT MEMBERSHIP against the metas' `inputs` lists, never entry-hood (a JSDoc-only edit to `src/domain/entities/npcs.js` stales two bundles). Every pre-proof measures it.

"""

ODQ = """- **§934.47 addendum 15 — THE CENSUS RECON EXECUTED: §21 AMENDED BY WHAT THE PIPELINE ACTUALLY DOES; EM-B2a's PREMISE REFUTED A TRAIN EARLY (__STAMP__; the successor chair, under the owner's delegation; vetoable).** An Opus recon ran the ruled measurement over all 525 golden rows with two instruments that never disagreed, and passed its control (the population step draws 315 unpinned, 0 under full pins; the loader moves no generated byte). CONFIRMED of §21: execution sees what no spelling can, and `(step, key)` is total against `getStepMeta()`. REFUTED or completed, and ruled in design §21.5: Tier 1 is 75 rows (five multi-producer keys; 18 mutates rows), 13 of 22 steps draw, 29 rows drawn / 46 pure; a key that stores a stream LABEL is a false "drawn" (`powerIntent`); ⭐ THE POWER STRUCTURE CONSUMES NO ENTROPY, so "root means chosen by a draw" is false of four of EM-A1's ten fields — DESIGN §14 IS AMENDED: an editable root is a fact the record HOLDS, whatever first produced it (`origin: drawn | computed` is recorded, never required), and a pin applies to a computed key as to a drawn one; "reaches the record" has three states (absent · same · TRANSFORMED); ⛔ PINNING FROM A RECORD REPRODUCES THE RECORD IN 2 OF 9 ROWS AND LETS `corruptionPass` WRITE INTO THE CALLER'S OWN RECORD IN 3 OF 9 — EM-P0's A2/A6 pin from the context and cannot see it — so EM-B2a IS BLOCKED and the chair opens ARCH-REDERIVE (which value a pin holds; pins final and isolated; multi-producer keys; mutating drawers; intra-step dependence), absorbing EM-P0b, after a focused recon on `assembleSettlement`'s enrichment; there is a HASH channel the draw census cannot see (`pickVariant`, 96 choices per settlement) and ⭐ it answers §934.52's owed measurement: a rename DOES re-roll — the institution's description, the relationship prose and the map glyph are keyed on display names — so those three sites join EM-P1b and EM-B1c's renames wait on it; a `pure` verdict carries its row count, the census corpus is the recon's 63-row sample plus an off-corpus random-mode block (five `resolveConfig` keys are pure over all 525 rows and drawn under the wizard's random modes), and mints are censused by execution (35 per run against 8 static spellings). EM-P2 version 3 is now compiled against this.
- **§934.47 addendum 16 — THE THREE PRE-PROOFS, AND WHAT PRICING THE BUDGETS BOUGHT (__STAMP__; the successor chair; vetoable).** EM-B3a READY-able: its window is empty, the scanner it rests on is now migration 202, it owes NO bundle budget — and its own STOP list forbade the order the train plan builds it in; RULED: the veil precedes the writer by design (EM-B2a and EM-C1 depend on it), the keys' inner shapes are opaque to it, and EM-B3c is chartered for the SQL-side subset arm. EM-P3 READY-able: as compiled it would have put +634 B into the ZERO-SLACK generation worker for a citation map the worker never reads — a certain terminal red, found on paper; RULED: the cure is the placement (the map moves to the domain leaf; the eager first-paint set must stay byte-identical at 268 or the lane stops), the remaining rise rides the standing conditional ruling. EM-B1d READY-able: its Markdown was still the pre-ruling EIGHT-file document while its manifest named five (the validator never compares the two — the implementer would have edited three unreserved files); it owes an EDGE-SHARED dirty build the compile had priced backwards (input membership, not entry-hood: a JSDoc-only edit to `npcs.js` stales two bundles) — a TENTH registration cost the EM preamble now names; RULED: token-membership matching with the foreign unions declared by name; writer-reach movement is the chair's to bank; the legacy spellings' availability is ratified as inert; the STALE EM-P2 v2 is withdrawn to the kit at B1d's placement.
"""

s = open(d, encoding="utf-8").read()
assert "### 21.5 " not in s
status_anchor = "**Status.** EM-P2 is STALE at the build lane's STOP;"
assert s.count(status_anchor) == 1
s = s.replace(status_anchor, DESIGN.replace("__STAMP__", stamp).lstrip("\n") + "\n" + status_anchor)
m14 = "## 14. Edit at the source, never at the derivation"
assert s.count(m14) == 1
i = s.index(m14); j = s.index("\n", i)
s = s[:j + 1] + "\n⚠ AMENDED BY §21.5.3 (measured): an editable root is a fact the record HOLDS — `origin: drawn | computed` is recorded per fact and is never the test of editability (the power structure consumes no entropy at generation, and the DM still seats a mayor).\n" + s[j + 1:]
open(d, "w", encoding="utf-8").write(s)

t = open(c, encoding="utf-8").read()
anchor = "## Pre-proof tasks (Opus, read-only, before each packet is READY)"
assert t.count(anchor) == 1
open(c, "w", encoding="utf-8").write(t.replace(anchor, CHARTER.replace("__STAMP__", stamp) + anchor))

o = open(f, encoding="utf-8").read().rstrip("\n")
open(f, "w", encoding="utf-8").write(o + "\n" + ODQ.replace("__STAMP__", stamp))
print("design §21.5 + §14 marker; charter amendments; ODQ addenda 15-16 written")
